IMPORT `nii-rounding-regulations`
IMPORT `nii-s381-rounding`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests: s 381 and the Rounding Regulations 5746-1985. Row IL-33.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew (regulation 1, line 16; regulation 2, line 23;
-- regulation 3, line 27; regulation 7, line 44) before the run.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — regulation 1: to whole new shekels (under 50 agorot dropped, 50 or more counts as a shekel)`

#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` 113.4 EQUALS 113
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` 113.49 EQUALS 113
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` 113.5 EQUALS 114
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` 113.99 EQUALS 114
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` 113 EQUALS 113
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` 0.49 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` 0.5 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` 0 EQUALS 0
-- The child allowance's multiplied amounts (s 68(b), 2026 basic amount 173): 2.24 x 173 = 387.52, 2.36 x 173 = 408.28.
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` (173 TIMES 2.24) EQUALS 388
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` (173 TIMES 2.36) EQUALS 408
-- The s 68(c) supplement (70% of 162 = 113.4; of 158 = 110.6).
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` (162 TIMES 0.7) EQUALS 113
#ASSERT `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` (158 TIMES 0.7) EQUALS 111
-- A negative amount is outside the Regulations.
#ASSERT REFUSED `reg 1 — rounded to whole new shekels:` (0 MINUS 1)

§ `Tests — regulation 2: a daily amount computed on income, to the agora`

#ASSERT `reg 2 — rounded to the agora:` 12.344 EQUALS 12.34
#ASSERT `reg 2 — rounded to the agora:` 12.345 EQUALS 12.35
#ASSERT `reg 2 — rounded to the agora:` 12.3449 EQUALS 12.34
#ASSERT `reg 2 — rounded to the agora:` 0.005 EQUALS 0.01
#ASSERT `reg 2 — rounded to the agora:` 0.0049 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 2 — rounded to the agora:` 12.34 EQUALS 12.34

§ `Tests — regulation 7: an addition, fine or overpayment ending in less than a shekel, rounded down`

#ASSERT `reg 7 — rounded down to the whole new shekel:` 12.99 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `reg 7 — rounded down to the whole new shekel:` 12.01 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `reg 7 — rounded down to the whole new shekel:` 12 EQUALS 12

§ `Tests — by the kind of amount`

#ASSERT `reg 2 to 7 — the amount rounded as the Regulations round a` `a daily benefit, or another daily payment of the Institute, computed on income, regulation 2` `:` 12.345 EQUALS 12.35
#ASSERT `reg 2 to 7 — the amount rounded as the Regulations round a` `a cash benefit, including a child allowance for each child and a dependants' supplement, regulation 3` `:` 387.52 EQUALS 388
#ASSERT `reg 2 to 7 — the amount rounded as the Regulations round a` `a monthly income used as the base of a benefit, or an amount that fixes entitlement to a payment or its rate, regulation 4` `:` 8000.5 EQUALS 8001
#ASSERT `reg 2 to 7 — the amount rounded as the Regulations round a` `an amount collected from a person liable for maintenance, regulation 5` `:` 1200.49 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `reg 2 to 7 — the amount rounded as the Regulations round a` `an amount used in charging insurance contributions, regulation 6` `:` 100.5 EQUALS 101
#ASSERT `reg 2 to 7 — the amount rounded as the Regulations round a` `an addition, a fine, an overpayment, ending in less than one new shekel, regulation 7` `:` 100.99 EQUALS 100

§ `Tests — s 381: which rules govern`

-- An amount under this Law: the Regulations govern whatever another law says.
#ASSERT `s 381 — the Rounding Regulations govern an amount, it being` TRUE `and the other law having its own provision:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 381 — the Rounding Regulations govern an amount, it being` TRUE `and the other law having its own provision:` FALSE
-- An amount under another law: the Regulations govern unless that law has its own provision.
#ASSERT `s 381 — the Rounding Regulations govern an amount, it being` FALSE `and the other law having its own provision:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 381 — the Rounding Regulations govern an amount, it being` FALSE `and the other law having its own provision:` TRUE

§ `Tests — regulation 3: the child allowance for each child`

-- A child who has no supplement: the allowance rounded.
#ASSERT `reg 3 — the allowance for one child, rounded:` (`The allowance for one child, before rounding` WITH `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b)` IS 173, `the supplement under section 68(c)` IS 0) EQUALS 173
-- 2026, a fourth child born before 1 June 2003 (s 68(b)(2): 173 x 2.24 = 387.52) with the supplement
-- (70% x 162 = 113.4). As one amount: 387.52 + 113.4 = 500.92 -> 501. On its own: 388 + 113 = 501. Same: answered.
#ASSERT `reg 3 — the allowance for one child, rounded:` (`The allowance for one child, before rounding` WITH `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b)` IS 173 TIMES 2.24, `the supplement under section 68(c)` IS 162 TIMES 0.7) EQUALS 501
-- 2026, a third child: 219 + 113.4 = 332.4 -> 332; 219 + 113 = 332. Same.
#ASSERT `reg 3 — the allowance for one child, rounded:` (`The allowance for one child, before rounding` WITH `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b)` IS 219, `the supplement under section 68(c)` IS 162 TIMES 0.7) EQUALS 332
-- 2025 figures, a fourth child born before 1 June 2003: 169 x 2.24 = 378.56 and 70% x 158 = 110.6. As one
-- amount: 489.16 -> 489. On its own: 379 + 111 = 490. They differ: declined by default.
#ASSERT REFUSED `reg 3 — the allowance for one child, rounded:` (`The allowance for one child, before rounding` WITH `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b)` IS 169 TIMES 2.24, `the supplement under section 68(c)` IS 158 TIMES 0.7)
#ASSERT `reg 3 — the allowance for one child, rounded, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `the child allowance and the supplement of section 68(c), for rounding` `read as` `the supplement is rounded with the allowance as one amount`) `:` (`The allowance for one child, before rounding` WITH `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b)` IS 169 TIMES 2.24, `the supplement under section 68(c)` IS 158 TIMES 0.7) EQUALS 489
#ASSERT `reg 3 — the allowance for one child, rounded, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `the child allowance and the supplement of section 68(c), for rounding` `read as` `the supplement is rounded on its own`) `:` (`The allowance for one child, before rounding` WITH `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b)` IS 169 TIMES 2.24, `the supplement under section 68(c)` IS 158 TIMES 0.7) EQUALS 490
-- A family of four, 2026: 173, 219, and the third and fourth at 219 with the supplement 113.4. Before rounding
-- the total is 173 + 219 + 332.4 + 332.4 = 1056.8. Each child rounded: 173 + 219 + 332 + 332 = 1056. (The total
-- rounded as one amount would be 1057, which regulation 3 does not do: it rounds the allowance "for each child".)
GIVEN b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The allowance for one child, before rounding`
`an allowance of` b `with supplement` c MEANS
    `The allowance for one child, before rounding` WITH `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b)` IS b, `the supplement under section 68(c)` IS c

#ASSERT `reg 3 — the total of the allowances for the children, each rounded:` (LIST `an allowance of` 173 `with supplement` 0, `an allowance of` 219 `with supplement` 0, `an allowance of` 219 `with supplement` (162 TIMES 0.7), `an allowance of` 219 `with supplement` (162 TIMES 0.7)) EQUALS 1056
-- The empty family.
#ASSERT `reg 3 — the total of the allowances for the children, each rounded:` (EMPTY) EQUALS 0

§ `Tests — a benefit under Chapter 8 (the Regulations' Chapter 6C), which regulation 3 leaves out`

-- Regulation 3 rounds a cash benefit "except a benefit under Chapter 6C of the Law" (line 27), which is today's Chapter 8
-- (the Law's text marks Chapter 8 with its old number). No other rule rounds it: refused by name, not rounded.
#ASSERT REFUSED `reg 2 to 7 — the amount rounded as the Regulations round a` `a benefit under Chapter 8 of the Law (insolvency proceedings; the Regulations' Chapter 6C), which regulation 3 leaves out` `:` 1234.56
